   <dataStore name="SYS-FAP accounting and position state"
               id="_65251bcf-30dd-434d-b7d6-213e95c21714"
               isUnlimited="false"/>
   <collaboration id="Collaboration_2592a405-fbef-4ab5-9893-5494369ac7d8"
                   name="CSP-BPMN-L2-001 - Process New-Trade Booking"
                   isClosed="false">
      <documentation><![CDATA[Purpose: Represent the detailed current-state activities, controls, decisions, system processing, and exception routing required to book new FX Forward records in SYS-FAP.
 
Parent model: CSP-BPMN-L1-001 - Manage FX Forward Current-State Lifecycle.
 
Coverage: CSP-PR-001; CSP-NT-002 through CSP-NT-013.
 
CSP-NT-001 - Generate and make the scheduled trade extract available - is represented directly in the parent Level 1 model and is therefore not executed again in this Level 2 process.
 
Primary input: CSP-IO-001 - Scheduled TBS trade extract.
 
Supporting inputs: CSP-IO-002 - Approved FAP import template; CSP-IO-003 - Approved mapping and reference rules.
 
Outputs: CSP-IO-004 through CSP-IO-008.
 
Source baseline: DOC-CSP-001 version 0.3, Git commit aef34bb
 
Scope: Current state only. SYS-INT and target-state orchestration capabilities are excluded.]]></documentation>
